{"id":"rajasthan-road-trip","title":"Rajasthan road trip","who":"Classic route · forts and desert by car","when":"October to March","vehicle":"Car (often with a driver), 10–14 days","kind":"car","color":"#e11d48","summary":"The pink, blue, golden and white cities of Rajasthan: Jaipur's palaces, Pushkar's lake, Jodhpur under Mehrangarh fort, Jaisalmer's sandstone citadel in the Thar desert, the Jain temples of Ranakpur and the hill walls of Kumbhalgarh, ending by the lakes of Udaipur.","sources":[{"label":"The Travel Blog: three weeks in Rajasthan","url":"https://thetravelblog.at/magic-of-india-a-3-week-rajasthan-travel-guide"},{"label":"Frommer's: planning a trip to Rajasthan","url":"https://www.frommers.com/destinations/rajasthan/planning-a-trip"}],"approximate":"A common loop; the roads are the router's choice.","km":1274,"bbox":[70.7599,24.5787,75.8197,27.0978],"stops":[{"name":"Jaipur","place":"Jaipur, Rajasthan","at":[26.9155,75.819],"text":"The pink city: Hawa Mahal, the City Palace and Amber Fort on its hill.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/East_facade_Hawa_Mahal_Jaipur_from_ground_level_%28July_2022%29_-_img_01.jpg/500px-East_facade_Hawa_Mahal_Jaipur_from_ground_level_%28July_2022%29_-_img_01.jpg","page":"Hawa Mahal","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_facade_Hawa_Mahal_Jaipur_from_ground_level_%28July_2022%29_-_img_01.jpg","credit":"Chainwit.","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Pushkar","place":"Pushkar, Rajasthan","at":[26.4876,74.5578],"text":"A holy lake ringed by bathing ghats; the camel fair in November.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Pushkar.jpg/500px-Pushkar.jpg","page":"Pushkar","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pushkar.jpg","credit":"Bernard Gagnon","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Jodhpur","place":"Jodhpur, Rajasthan","at":[26.2968,73.0351],"text":"The blue city below Mehrangarh, one of India's mightiest forts.","source":{"